Attribution notice

GPTWorker is built in part on code from
hoangcoderr/chatgpt-local-coder. Active reused and modified portions include
the local coding runtime and supporting helpers, including:

- the patch application engine;
- MCP session/transport handling and recovery logic;
- shared tool-result and MCP annotation helpers;
- the activity/runtime logging foundation;
- portions of the filesystem/search and local worker/tunnel runtime that
  remain derived from Local Coder.

These inherited portions have been modified and integrated into GPTWorker's
current architecture.

GPTWorker-specific code, including its Job lifecycle, confirmed-Workspace
boundary, execution-authority model, lazy runtime-family loading, control
surface, and other new orchestration/runtime behavior, is copyright
thebimhouseinfo-sudo and GPTWorker contributors.
